# Restart RescueTemple after a ticket

When you **finish implementing a ticket** (Linear/GitHub issue work is done, tests green, UI wired), **force-close RescueTemple and open it again** before ending the turn. Do this even if hot reload is already running.

## How

1. Kill the Windows editor process (ignore failure if it is not running):
   `/mnt/c/Windows/System32/taskkill.exe /F /IM RescueTemple.exe`
2. Also kill leftover `dotnet watch` for RescueTemple if it would keep the old binary locked.
3. Relaunch with `./RescueEditor/dev.sh` from the repo root (background it; that script already taskkills `RescueTemple.exe` and starts Windows hot reload).
4. If Windows .NET / the `pmd-red-win` mirror is unavailable, use `./RescueEditor/dev.sh --linux`.

Do **not** skip this because “watch should pick up the change.” The user wants a full process restart so they see the new build.